 ## Distribution limitations accepted
 
 The rule itself allows more than the current fixed colors, opposite-corner presentation, and 3×3 normalized shape universe might suggest. I accepted that bounded domain because it is constructive, diverse enough for the repository gates, canonical-compatible, and semantically strong; I did not claim it covers the full lawful input space. A future expansion should vary legal spatial relations and larger normalized shapes while retaining explicit witnesses and avoiding search/fallback control flow.
+
+## Reviewer follow-up — position can masquerade as semantic role (2026-10-24)
+
+A source-pinned protected-Racket probe retained a three-demonstration lesson in
+which every visible example uses `placement=red_nw`.  The executable wrong rule
+`northwest_object_is_red_role` ignores colors and assigns output roles by object
+position; it fits all three demonstrations, the current `lesson_identifiable`
+checker returns no reasons, and a `red_se` query differs in 6 cells.  Evidence:
+`checks/9e47b59d6afc/position-role-witness.json`; reusable probe:
+`workspace/lesson_probe.py`.  Production bytes remain unchanged.  The concrete
+repair is to add this position-role rival to the lesson competitor inventory or
+require visible role-placement reversal before lesson admission.  This is one
+bounded witness, not a universal ambiguity claim.
